  "published": "2026-11-11T10:29:41.84Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v0.5.0: Release-blocking engine fixes and keyed-service semantics. First version published to nuget.org after 0.2.0 (0.3.0 and 0.4.0 never shipped because CI failed), so it also carries everything listed under v0.4.0 and v0.3.0.\n\nAdded:\n  * RegisterDecorator(Type serviceType, Type decoratorType) on IContainerBuilder, so open-generic decorators (IRepository<> -> LoggingRepository<>) are reachable from the public API. An open-generic decorator also wraps closed-only base registrations.\n  * ServiceNotRegisteredException.Key; the keyed-miss message now names the key.\n\nFixed:\n  * A singleton whose construction throws is retried on the next resolve instead of replaying the cached exception.\n  * Same-thread singleton cycles throw CircularDependencyException (not InvalidOperationException); a cross-thread singleton cycle is detected and reported instead of deadlocking.\n  * ResolveKeyed / TryResolveKeyed find keyed open-generic registrations and keyed registrations added to a child scope via BeginLifetimeScope.\n  * TryResolve / ResolveOptional of Lazy<T>, Func<T>, Owned<T> answer false / null when T is not registered (Owned<T> used to throw; Lazy/Func used to fail later on use).\n\nChanged:\n  * Keyed registrations are no longer the default: Resolve<T>() and IEnumerable<T> / ResolveAll<T>() skip WithKey(...) registrations, and IsRegistered<T>() answers for unkeyed registrations only. Keyed services stay reachable via ResolveKeyed / TryResolveKeyed / ResolveDictionary. This restores Microsoft.Extensions.DependencyInjection keyed-service semantics through the sidecar.\n\nv0.4.0: Engine hardening, faster resolution, and a richer resolution API.\n\nAdded:\n  * Public keyed resolution: ResolveKeyed<T>(key), ResolveKeyed(Type, key), TryResolveKeyed<T>(key, out value) on IResolver.\n  * Non-throwing resolution: TryResolve<T>(out value) and ResolveOptional<T>() (plus Type overloads).\n  * Registration probe: IContainer.IsRegistered<T>() / IsRegistered(Type).\n  * Open-generic decorators: RegisterDecorator on an open generic now wraps closed resolutions; decorators are pre-indexed by service type.\n  * Non-public [Inject] methods are now invoked, matching property injection.\n\nFixed / changed:\n  * Concurrency: _byServiceType is a ConcurrentDictionary, fixing a data race when open generics are closed under concurrent load.\n  * Singletons are constructed exactly once under parallel resolution.\n  * Lock-free activator caches plus a registration-lookup-before-collection fast path cut per-resolve overhead and lock contention.\n  * Func<T> / Lazy<T> / Func<P, T> activators are cached (Func<P, T> no longer recompiles its expression per resolve).\n\nFor ASP.NET Core / Generic Host integration use the TechTeaStudio.Injector.Extensions.DependencyInjection sidecar package.\n\nFull changelog: https://github.com/TechTeaStudio/Injector/blob/product/CHANGELOG.md",
